    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 518,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Capital Press\nThe Capital Press is a weekly agricultural newspaper covering the West Coast of the United States , and published in Salem , Oregon . The newspaper covers farming , ranching and agriculture industries in the Pacific Northwest . The newspaper is owned by the EO Media Group . The paper was established in February 1928 as the Hollywood Press by Abner M. Church as a community newspaper serving a portion of Oregon 's capital city . The name of the newspaper was changed in December 1932 to Capital Press ."
